diff --git a/SSBM_ORACLE.md b/SSBM_ORACLE.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..642b59b73
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SSBM_ORACLE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Headless SSBM validation oracle
+
+This fork adds bounded read-only frame/RNG captures and an explicit arithmetic
+profile to the upstream exi-ai-rebase headless runner. It does not replace game
+logic. Original source license terms remain in force.
+
+Set `SSBM_ORACLE_ARITHMETIC=deterministic` before launching
+`dolphin-emu-nogui` to disable host FMA generation before JIT initialization.
+This selects the separately rounded multiply/add path used by the interpreter.
+The default is `host-default`, preserving upstream host-dependent behavior.
+Every launch logs the requested mode and effective host FMA flag. Unknown
+profile values are rejected with exit code 2 before booting a game.
+
+The explicit setting avoids using movie/netplay determinism flags, whose other
+state requirements are inappropriate for standalone Slippi playback.
+
+Validation: the same replay, ISO, binary and inputs give Nana's frame-20 Y as
+29.769750595092773 in deterministic mode, matching its recorded Slippi state
+and CPUCore=0 interpreter. Host-default yields 29.769752502441406 on the tested
+FMA-capable host. This is bounded regression evidence, not full-match parity.
+No replay data or disc assets are distributed with this fork.
